{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PairwiseChainLeadingOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.PairwiseChainLeadingOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_ratios_T_He3_not_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_ratios_T_He3_not_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L240-L264","doc":"**The `T` and `³He` chain-over-atom ratios really do depend on the ordering.**\n\nStated as a **disequality** so it cannot be read as a claim about which value is\nright — both are correct, for their own word.\n\n    T     292/163 ≈ 1.7914  (grouped)  →  4      (Borromean)\n    ³He    30/17  ≈ 1.7647  (grouped)  →  3/2    (Borromean)\n\nThis is the counterpoint that gives `chain_over_atom_He4_of_letters` its force.\nThere the `(a + b)` cancels identically, so ⁴He's `24/7` holds for **every**\nletter weighting and survives any intra-nucleon reordering. `T` and `³He` have\n`Z ≠ N`, no such cancellation, and move — so the ⁴He invariance is a property of\nthat combination, not a general feature of the chain ratios.\n\nAdded on top of the `qou-j1e5` derivation rather than alongside it: a parallel\nbranch (`qou-pdg9`, PR #6920) reached the same generic `24/7` independently and\ndeferred to this file, and this disequality is the one statement that branch had\nwhich this file did not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_grouped_values_eq_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_grouped_values_eq_closed","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L229-L238","doc":"The same closed form at the **superseded** grouped weights reproduces the\nsix grouped values, which is what makes the ordering change a change of two\ncoefficients rather than of the derivation. Kept as a check on that claim, not\nas a live model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_defs_eq_closed_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_defs_eq_closed_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L220-L227","doc":"The closed form at the Borromean weights reproduces all six definitions\nabove. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He4_of_letters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He4_of_letters","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L207-L218","doc":"**The `⁴He` chain-over-atom ratio is `24/7` for every `(a, b)`.**\n\nThe `(a + b)` cancels identically, so the ratio does not depend on the letter\nweights at all — hence it is the same under the grouped weights `(21, 16)` and\nthe Borromean weights `(3, −2)`, and the `37` that appeared to cancel\n\"strikingly\" in the older reading is simply `a + b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he4_of_letters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he4_of_letters","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L199-L205","doc":"The `⁴He` atom term is `7(a+b)/128`. This is where the `7` in `259 = 7·37`\ncomes from — it is `2^-5 − 2^-8` times two, not a property of `37`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pairSum_of_letters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pairSum_of_letters","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L191-L197","doc":"The three pair terms sum to `3(a+b)/16`, the `+1` and `−1` interface\ncontributions of `pp` and `nn` cancelling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1Closed","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L181-L189","doc":"The closed form of the leading coefficient at letter weights `(a, b)`:\n\n    c₁(Z,N) = (a·Z + b·N)(2^-(A+1) − 2^-2A) − 4(i_pp − i_nn)·2^-2A\n\nwith `A = Z + N`, `i_pp = max(Z−1, 0)`, `i_nn = max(N−1, 0)`. Natural subtraction\nalready truncates at zero, so `Z - 1` *is* `i_pp`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chains_overcount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chains_overcount","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L166-L172","doc":"All three chains over-count: every leading-order ratio exceeds `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He4_gt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He4_gt_three","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**The leading-order error is large.** At `⁴He` the pairwise chain exceeds the\nexact `H_{3A}` trace by more than a factor of three as `ℏ_q → 0`.\n\nThis is the formal statement of the warning in the header: the ratio measured at\n`q₀` is not a leading-order property, so the pairwise approximation is not\ncontrolled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He4","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L150-L154","doc":"**`⁴He`: exactly `24/7`.** Proved structurally below\n(`chain_over_atom_He4_of_letters`) — it is the same value under the grouped\nweights and under the Borromean ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_He3","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L146-L148","doc":"**`³He`: exactly `3/2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_over_atom_T","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L142-L144","doc":"**Tritium: the chain over-counts by exactly `4`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_He4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_He4","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L137-L140","doc":"The `⁴He` chain sum at leading order. Equal to the `³He` sum, since the `nn`\nbond contributes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_He3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_He3","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L133-L135","doc":"The `³He` chain sum at leading order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chain_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chain_T","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L128-L131","doc":"The tritium chain sum at leading order. With `c1_nn = 0` this is the `pn`\nbond alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_dyadic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_dyadic","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L114-L121","doc":"**Every one of them is dyadic**: multiplying by the right power of two gives\nan integer. Stated as `c₁ · 2^k = m` rather than via `Rat.den`, which does not\nreduce under `decide` for a division literal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_He4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_He4","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L111-L112","doc":"Leading `ℏ_q` coefficient for the whole `⁴He` braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_He3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_He3","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L108-L109","doc":"Leading `ℏ_q` coefficient for the whole `³He` braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_T","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L105-L106","doc":"Leading `ℏ_q` coefficient for the whole tritium braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_nn","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L101-L103","doc":"Leading `ℏ_q` coefficient for the `nn` bond. **Exactly zero** under the\nBorromean word — a vanishing coefficient, not a small one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_pn","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Leading `ℏ_q` coefficient for the `pn` bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.c1_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.c1_pp","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/PairwiseChainLeadingOrder.lean#L95-L96","doc":"Leading `ℏ_q` coefficient for the `pp` bond. ","signatureChunk":0}]}